          "path": "_m/r/j/p/7/daintree-national-park-wp/complex-mesophyll-vine-forest-.jpg",
          "filename": "Complex mesophyll vine forest Daintree National Park Queensland 1986 IMG 0002 (2).jpg",
          "caption": "Daintree National Park is a national park in Far North Queensland, Australia, 1,757 km (1,092 mi) northwest of Brisbane and 100 km (62 mi) northwest of Cairns. It was founded in 1981 and is part of the Wet Tropics of Queensland.  In 1988 it became a World Heritage Site. The park consists of two sections, with a settled agricultural area between them which includes the towns of Mossman and Daintree Village.",
